  "authoringNote": "Same encounter as F07d: C01 keeps day 29, so the inclusive bound is 2024-08-29; the leap day is not treated as a month end that moves the bound to 2024-08-31. The final order is dated 2024-08-30, one day after the bound, so the pair holds R04.order_after_bound, a conflict for the administrative reviewer. The order follows the encounter and the identifiers match, so no other R04 condition holds. R04 cites six facts and names no parent (C07). The receipt (2024-08-31T17:00:00Z) is after the order date span 2024-08-29T10:00Z to 2024-08-31T12:00Z (C06), so R05 passes. The case and explicit assessment date stay 2026-10-18 and the supplier interval 2026-01-01 to 2026-12-31 contains it; the older medical dates are synthetic arithmetic inputs only. No rule compares an order's age with the assessment date, no order-age limit is implied and no clinical or current-policy validity is claimed for an old order. R01, R02, R03, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_human_review.",
